# One scheme for every test (num-visc v1): HLL damping on the reconstructed jump in both channels (NUM_VISC_L = NUM_VISC_T = 0, no bare difference), regularised only by the quadratic artificial viscosity rho (4 dx)^2 |D| that vanishes as h^2; should give second-order waves and enough damping in the rod impact.
# Uniform choices (identical in every test): no tensile correction (GNOG 2 instead), matrix divergence (base), deviatoric force on the MFM face, 2D-traceless deviator as GIZMO, unlimited gradient in the stress rate, no adhesion between bodies, correct work-term sign, no physical viscosity.
RECON_FACE_DV 0
NUM_VISC 1
NUM_VISC_L 0.
NUM_VISC_T 0.
ART_VISC 1
ART_VISC_C 4.
TENSILE_CORRECTION 0
GNOG_PENALTY 2
ELASTIC_FACE_MODE 2
STRESS_2D_GIZMO 1
STRESS_RATE_RAW_GRAD 1
CONTACT_NO_TENSION 1
ELASTIC_WORK_SIGN_FIX 1
MATERIAL_VISCOSITY 0
